// MOVE 3b (move3-3 .. move3-6), Peng #10: the Third Phase Offensive, 31 Dec 1950 - 7 Jan 1951. Basemap seoul_hd_ref (z10, HD),
// winter (snow, cold grade). Fronts per date + sources: research/FACT_NOTES_seoul.md (tools/make_seoul_control.py).
//   move3-3  the UN line (option 2 glowing fronts, 26-31 Dec): US I + IX Corps divisions (big counters, tanks, guns, air support) and the
//            South Korean divisions between and beside them (thin counters); red belief card HOLD NORTH OF SEOUL; Peng: THE SEAMS;
//            the I/IX Corps boundary (ROK 1st + 6th Divs) glows white
//   move3-4  NIGHT 31 Dec (New Year's Eve): the 30-minute barrage (K.gun -> arc -> K.impact, shake), the 116th Div across the frozen
//            Imjin into the ROK 1st Div, the US 25th Div NOT ATTACKED, midnight: the 113th Div on the ROK 6th, 02:00 the 66th Army on
//            the ROK 5th (+ 2nd); before dawn the ROK 1st is driven out (the front band moves to the wedge)
//   move3-5  1 Jan morning: Ridgway's jeep north, ROK trucks streaming south, the open flanks of the US divisions, Chinese curling round
//   move3-6  1 Jan noon: back to the Seoul bridgehead; 3 Jan: ABANDON SEOUL; refugees over the ice (~600,000); the Han bridges blown
//            (impacts + shake); the British rear guard (UK flag) cut off; 4 Jan: the Seoul ring flips blue, SEOUL FALLS;
//            zoom out (option 1, 7 Jan): LINE D Pyongtaek - Ansong - Changhowon-ni - Wonju
// Built with: python3 tools/build_scene.py move3b seoul_hd_ref move3-3 move3-6
